{"data": [{"author_id": "2116622308999876608", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:14:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117425155160858726"], "id": "2117425155160858726", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick The fairest meetup spot feature is the kind of tiny tool people would actually pay for. Great example of a weekend build with a real use.", "url": "https://x.com/prompstoprofit/status/2117425155160858726"}, {"author_id": "371091579", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:12:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117424562828636242"], "id": "2117424562828636242", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick What stands out is how short the loop from idea to polished interactive site has become. The scarce skill now is deciding what's worth building and checking the data underneath it.", "url": "https://x.com/itsmeandresito/status/2117424562828636242"}, {"author_id": "1499198533106540546", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:06:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117423139659608533"], "id": "2117423139659608533", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Finally, a scientific way to prove my friends should be the ones driving to me.", "url": "https://x.com/ajutqs/status/2117423139659608533"}, {"author_id": "1464292909952516102", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:05:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422833899028845"], "id": "2117422833899028845", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick This is how you sell AI to normal people.\nNot a chatbot. A useful thing they can click.\nDemos like this change more minds than any benchmark.", "url": "https://x.com/mvxswell/status/2117422833899028845"}, {"author_id": "1616553472207523840", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:03:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422503551545846"], "id": "2117422503551545846", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Neat use of a coding model for something actually useful. A fairest-meeting-point calculator over real road routes is the kind of small tool I'd want to poke at with my own city pairs.", "url": "https://x.com/chnhn05782803/status/2117422503551545846"}, {"author_id": "2953739684", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:03:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117422316519125327"], "id": "2117422316519125327", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick The \"fairest place to meet\" feature is a great example of a tool nobody would build by hand, but an AI will in an afternoon.\n\nHow many rounds of iteration did it take to get the routing data right?", "url": "https://x.com/AzrianoY1/status/2117422316519125327"}, {"author_id": "1145463968573599744", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:24:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117412664502583438"], "id": "2117412664502583438", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick This is the kind of build more people should try. Pick an old site you loved that died and ask the model to remake it, you learn way more doing that than building another todo app", "url": "https://x.com/global_techgirl/status/2117412664502583438"}, {"author_id": "1039925196386226178", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:19:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117411271285043664"], "id": "2117411271285043664", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick This is so addicting to play with", "url": "https://x.com/_DMontgomery40/status/2117411271285043664"}, {"author_id": "1471500379296727055", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:41:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117401673715126762"], "id": "2117401673715126762", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick That’s really cool", "url": "https://x.com/Dyslexic_iRobot/status/2117401673715126762"}, {"author_id": "1519346231272685568", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:36:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117400403092410772"], "id": "2117400403092410772", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 51, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Please share the prompt . It’s be great to run this for all countries .", "url": "https://x.com/HasanASaleem/status/2117400403092410772"}, {"author_id": "1921273778664882177", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:25:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117397603122077983"], "id": "2117397603122077983", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117208259438522371", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Two perfectly optimized routes can still send everyone to a badly chosen meeting place.\n\nYour meetup feature fixes the decision before optimizing the trip. I wrote about the same mistake with AI assignments: https://t.co/0Q5rRBScZm", "url": "https://x.com/Oldnoob007/status/2117397603122077983"}, {"author_id": "46498861", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:20:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117396530663706691"], "id": "2117396530663706691", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick This is where these tools quietly change who gets to explore data. A question that once needed a small team and a free month becomes an evening project, and the bottleneck moves to having the question.", "url": "https://x.com/raulnogales/status/2117396530663706691"}, {"author_id": "1622058248953020418", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:01:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117391679896584451"], "id": "2117391679896584451", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick The watershed view of big cities is a fun surprise. It's a good example of how cheap it's become to turn a quirky idea into a working interactive site in an afternoon.", "url": "https://x.com/AiOffers/status/2117391679896584451"}, {"author_id": "1337419042085277696", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:00:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117391534483988749"], "id": "2117391534483988749", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 35, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick the wild part is people who can't code can get stuff like this built now. I'm one of them. deciding what's worth building is the hard part", "url": "https://x.com/ReneChavez_wooo/status/2117391534483988749"}, {"author_id": "21230558", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:29:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117383646353195246"], "id": "2117383646353195246", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 195, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick half the fun now is dead old sites coming back because someone got curious one afternoon", "url": "https://x.com/csudheera/status/2117383646353195246"}, {"author_id": "1752307409186361344", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:23:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117382173909262371"], "id": "2117382173909262371", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 268, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick The 'fairest place to meet up' map is going to end more friendships than it saves.", "url": "https://x.com/KubalaChase/status/2117382173909262371"}, {"author_id": "1642137369569820672", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:15:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117380095010824368"], "id": "2117380095010824368", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Routing and fair meetup points are classic graph problems, so I'd be curious whether Opus wrote its own shortest-path code or leaned on an existing routing library. That choice decides how much to trust the edge cases like ferries and seasonal roads.", "url": "https://x.com/surveywork0/status/2117380095010824368"}, {"author_id": "2110550226989711360", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:15:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117380009127968777"], "id": "2117380009127968777", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick rebuilding dead tools is such an underrated use. if there's an old site you miss, describe what it used to do and ask Claude for a simple version as an artifact, you can usually use it right there in the chat", "url": "https://x.com/plainAItips/status/2117380009127968777"}, {"author_id": "14180572", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:07:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117377982834860472"], "id": "2117377982834860472", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick Me and my friends just drive to our local airports, catch a flight, then meet up somewhere.", "url": "https://x.com/john_dough/status/2117377982834860472"}, {"author_id": "365125035", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:06:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117377941650935873"], "id": "2117377941650935873", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 198, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick gonna pull up the watersheds view for dfw just to confirm what I already know… every road ends in a traffic jam on 35", "url": "https://x.com/ThatGuySizemore/status/2117377941650935873"}, {"author_id": "2116355353327587329", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:05:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117377605603340649"], "id": "2117377605603340649", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick The \"fairest place to meet\" view is the sneaky useful one. Weighting by actual drive time instead of straight-line distance changes the answer a lot for anyone near mountains or water.", "url": "https://x.com/XWolfHQ/status/2117377605603340649"}, {"author_id": "1363491876", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:05:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117377580290420970"], "id": "2117377580290420970", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick The watersheds view is the clever part, since it turns a pile of drive-time data into something you can read at a glance. How much of the routing did Opus write itself versus pulling from an existing engine like OSRM?", "url": "https://x.com/0xCryptoFishy/status/2117377580290420970"}, {"author_id": "1599103834554437632", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:00:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117376295877357826"], "id": "2117376295877357826", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick This is super cool.", "url": "https://x.com/James1Mclendon/status/2117376295877357826"}, {"author_id": "1027553127128428544", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:58:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117375889717801208"], "id": "2117375889717801208", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick The fairest-meeting-point map is the one I'd use first.\n\nDid Opus pull real road network data for the routes, or estimate drive times some other way? That decides how far I'd trust the watershed view", "url": "https://x.com/raja_sudireddy/status/2117375889717801208"}, {"author_id": "1995839988760805379", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:49:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117373438138421667"], "id": "2117373438138421667", "in_reply_to_user_id": "39125788", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117346417979384162", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@emollick The gap between what these models can do and what most people actually ask them to do is getting bigger and bigger…", "url": "https://x.com/rozzabuilds/status/2117373438138421667"}], "includes": {"tweets": [{"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:01:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117